# models/discover

The posts the maintainer has put on the public Discover page,
blot.im/discover (#2639). Discover is one list for all of blot.im, so its keys
are not under any blog.

## Keys

| Key | Type | What |
|-----|------|------|
| `discover:posts` | sorted set | Post IDs, scored by when the maintainer added each post (ms). The page reads it newest first. |
| `discover:post:<id>` | hash | `blogID`, `entryID` (the entry's path), `photos` (JSON) and `added`. |
| `discover:blog:<blogID>` | set | A blog's post IDs, so they can be removed together. |
| `discover:token:<token>` | string | `{ blogID, entryID }` for an "Add to Discover" link, expiring after 24 hours. |

A post's ID is a hash of its blog ID and entry path (`postID.js`).

## Live entries

Only the reference and the chosen photos are stored. `list.js` loads each
blog and entry as the page is read and leaves a post out while:

- its site is disabled, gone, or has `includeInDiscover` off;
- the entry is deleted, a draft, scheduled or has no URL;
- it had photos and none of the chosen ones are still in the entry's HTML.

So nothing stored changes when a site turns the setting off and on again,
or an author edits a post: the title and URL always come from the entry.

## Photos

`photos.candidates` lists the images in an entry's HTML which are the blog's
own generated assets on the CDN (`_image_cache/...`, `_thumbnails/...`).
Discover only reads those, from the storage bucket, and never fetches a URL
from a post. `photos.derive` resizes each chosen one to at most 1200px into
`{blogID}/_discover/<postID>/`, served from cdn.blot.im. No sweep lists
`_discover`, and blog deletion removes it with the rest of the blog's assets.

## Tokens

`token.create` is called by the daily update email for each new post from a
site with the setting on. `token.read` does not use the token up, because
mail scanners open links; `token.consume` deletes it with `GETDEL`, so only
one request can add the post.

## Working on the page locally

One command fills the local /discover with real posts:

    node scripts/discover/mirror-featured.js [host ...] [--limit <n>]

It copies each featured site's 10 newest posts and their images from its
public RSS feed (development only), keeping production's blog IDs, entry
URLs and image asset paths, and puts each site's newest post with photos on
Discover. Run it in the node container (`blot-node-<slot>` for a preview).

To pick posts by hand instead, `scripts/discover/add-links.js <host>` prints
"Add to Discover" links for a site's newest posts; locally any account can
open the manage page.

## Moving picks to production

`scripts/discover/export.js data/discover.json` writes the local picks,
identified by blog ID, entry URL and source image path. On production, after
`docker cp` of the file, `scripts/discover/import.js /tmp/discover.json`
checks them and `--apply` imports them: it finds each entry by URL, keeps the
photos still in the post, resizes production's own copies and keeps the
order. Posts already on Discover are skipped, so it is safe to re-run.
